  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 247 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nConditions generally are expected to remain dry Tuesday, outside of \nthe low potential for showers and weak storms to the west early on. \nSurface high pressure is forecast to track southeast into the Upper \nMidwest, with its influence generally over Iowa through Wednesday. \nTemperatures will be a touch cooler through midweek, with values in \nthe upper 80s to low 90s, and dewpoints in the 60s, ending the \nstretch of the dangerous heat. While another weak wave could bring \nanother low potential for rain in the western Central Plains \nWednesday morning, a more potent wave is signaled to descend on the \neastern fringe of the upper western ridge in the late work week, \nbringing some potential for more widespread shower and storm \nactivity then. Specific details will be better known in the coming \ndays as more data becomes available from additional model members. \nTemperatures look to trend cooler into next weekend, with average \nhighs in the low to mid 80s and dewpoints in the 60s, which will be \na welcome break from the previous heat.",
